title: 'Symbol layer team review: sound core, silent identity/freshness bugs → symbol integrity arc'
summary: 'The founder asked whether the symbol and mapping layer needs a large-scale upgrade. Three agents reviewed it in parallel (architect, reliability reviewer, efficiency/usage). Verdict: no rewrite. The foundations are deterministic and cheap (~125ms cold parse, 1,377 symbols), but identity, edges and freshness carry silent-wrong-answer bugs. Two were reproduced and verified by the lead. This led to TD-2026-10-13-661 and tasks T-2026-10-13-001/002/003. The session started from an external "Tier-1 knowledge graph / push not pull" reel, audited in neurons and discarded; push retrieval is deferred until after Phases 1–2.'
