decisions:
  - id: TD-2026-10-13-661
    decision: Three-phase symbol integrity arc; no rewrite
    rationale: Defects are local to identity/edges/freshness; the deterministic .purpose foundation is the moat
learnings:
  - 'VERIFIED: paradigm_ripple reports 0 dependents + ''safe to proceed'' for a portal.yaml gate referenced via a .purpose gates: list. aggregateFromDirectory emits both purpose-ref-gate-X (stub, first) and gate-X (portal). resolveReferences writes referencedBy onto the last (portal) entry; getSymbol returns the first (stub). Repro: a temp project with portal.yaml `gates: {authenticated: ...}` (gates are a MAP, not a list) plus a component `gates: [^authenticated]`.'
  - 'VERIFIED: the MCP server''s ctx.index is a startup snapshot, refreshed only by purpose-portal writes and paradigm_reindex. getLiveIndex (7.13) has one consumer: graph-slice. Hand edits and git checkouts are invisible to search, ripple and navigate.'
  - 'Reported by the reviewer, unreproduced: stubs mask dangling refs in the integrity checker; within-category duplicate IDs collapse silently (last wins); lookups are prefix/case-sensitive while search lowercases; several paths strip prefixes (#auth == ^auth); paradigm_reindex runs rebuildStaticFiles on the stale aggregation, then rebuilds again in the background.'
  - Edges are untyped and come from a regex over JSON.stringify(entry.data), so prose mentions become dependencies. There are three ripple implementations (MCP BFS 3-5, CLI 1-hop with a dead --depth, aspect-graph BFS) and they disagree.
  - 'Usage (216 sessions): related, graph ops and retrieve have 0 calls; the aspect search_log/search_weights/anchor_history tables have 0 rows; ripple has only 4 calls. Doctor takes 74.7s wall. 107/121 .purpose files parse, with 44 schema errors in 2 Conductor files.'
  - 'Don''t: no embeddings (TD-2026-09-29-204), no DB-first authoring, keep the five prefixes, wire the live index in rather than replace it.'
